#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1152
msgid "Block author enumeration"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1156
msgid "Redirects ?author=N and /author/slug/ probes from logged-out visitors to the home page, preventing usernames from being harvested for brute-force attacks. Also removes the users sitemap (wp-sitemap-users-1.xml) to close the same leak via sitemaps. Complements disabling the REST users endpoint."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1168
msgid "Disable Application Passwords"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1172
msgid "Removes the Application Passwords authentication method. These bypass two-factor authentication plugins. Warning: this will break any existing integration that authenticates with an application password. MainWP is unaffected — it uses its own signed channel."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:118
msgid "Present (enforcement unverified)"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1186
msgid "Disable XML-RPC"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1190
msgid "Disables the XML-RPC endpoint and pingback headers/methods."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1208
msgid "Block xmlrpc.php at server level"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1212
msgid "Layers a server-level 403 for xmlrpc.php on top of the PHP disable above — it does not replace it. When the vhost honors .htaccess the request is denied before PHP boots, turning a full WordPress bootstrap into a static denial (a performance win against brute-force and system.multicall floods); when .htaccess is inert the PHP disable still blocks XML-RPC, so you are never left unprotected. MainWP is unaffected — it uses its own signed HTTP channel, not XML-RPC."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:122
msgid "Unverified"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1227
msgid "Generic login error messages"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1231
msgid "Replaces login and password-reset error messages with a single generic string, so attackers cannot determine whether a username exists. Real users see a less specific message."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1245
msgid "Send security headers"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1249
msgid "Adds X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff, X-Frame-Options: SAMEORIGIN, a Referrer-Policy, COOP, CORP, and a configurable Permissions-Policy to front-end responses. Conservative defaults with no side effects. Content-Security-Policy is configured separately below."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:126
msgid "Enforcement has not been confirmed yet. Run \"Verify enforcement\" to probe whether the server is actually applying these rules."
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1281
msgid "HTTP Strict Transport Security"
msgstr ""

#: src/components/HardeningSettings.jsx:1285
msgid "Tells browsers to only ever connect to your site over HTTPS for a set duration, protecting against protocol-downgrade attacks and cookie hijacking on insecure networks. Only sent when the request is actually HTTPS (including behind a reverse proxy). Once a browser has seen this header, it will refuse plain HTTP connections until max-age expires — make sure HTTPS works reliably before enabling."
